  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R5", "R13"],
      "pins": ["U6.FB", "U6.SW"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "FB node (R5/R13/U6.FB)"],
      "observed": "In the power-train sheet the TPS62933 buck U6 output divider is drawn as R5 = 21k3 from the L1/+5V output node to the FB node and R13 = 10k from the FB node to GND.",
      "expected": "The TPS62933 regulates its FB pin to an internal 0.8 V reference, so for the specified +5 V output the top resistor must be about 52.3 kΩ with a 10 kΩ bottom (0.8 V x (1 + 52.3/10) = 5.0 V). 21.3 kΩ over 10 kΩ programs only about 2.5 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R5 21k3 ... R13 10k (TPS62933 output feedback divider, power-train sheet)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U1 — TPS62933 (TI) | 24 V → 5 V synchronous buck regulator, 3 A"}
      ],
      "impact": "The main +5V rail would sit near 2.5 V instead of 5 V, the AZ1117-3.3 LDO would drop out of regulation, and the ESP32-C6 DevKit, I2C pull-ups and TMC2209 logic (all derived from +5V/+3V3) would be starved; the board would not operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R3"],
      "pins": [],
      "nets": ["FLOAT_HIGH sense net"],
      "observed": "In the water-level/safety-switch block the FLOAT_HIGH sense line is pulled to GND through R3 = 1.0 kΩ (while the companion pull-up R26 on the other float input is 10 kΩ).",
      "expected": "The specification's float-switch network lists 'R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k', i.e. a 10 kΩ pull-down on FLOAT_HIGH (the FLOAT_LOW pull-up is also 10 kΩ). A 1.0 kΩ pull-down is ten times too small.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R26 10k ... R3 1.0k (safety-switch block, water level sensor/switches sheet)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R6 FLOAT_LOW +3V3 10k, R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k, R2 FLOAT_LOW /BPUMP 4.7k, R11 FLOAT_HIGH /BATO 4.7k"}
      ],
      "impact": "The FLOAT_HIGH input draws roughly 3.3 mA instead of 0.33 mA and, together with the 4.7 kΩ base resistor of the interlock transistor, shifts the float-switch threshold, giving a different (less reliable) high-level overflow interlock behaviour than intended.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic largely matches the specification, but the TPS62933 feedback divider (R5 = 21k3 over R13 = 10k) is set for ~2.5 V rather than the specified 5 V rail, which would leave the whole board under-powered, and the FLOAT_HIGH pull-down R3 is 1.0 kΩ where the spec calls for 10 kΩ."
}

